<p>President Trump said the United States has asked China to push back his planned March 31-April 2 visit to Beijing by about a month, saying he wants to stay in Washington while the war with Iran continues. The White House said he still looks forward to the trip and does not see the meeting as being in jeopardy, but the timing may shift because overseeing Operation Epic Fury is his top priority for now. The delay matters because the summit had been expected to help steady a difficult US-China relationship, already strained by trade disputes, Taiwan tensions and now the widening effects of the Iran war. Trump also publicly tied the trip to efforts to keep shipping moving through the Strait of Hormuz, where about one-fifth of the world’s oil passes each day. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent later described separate talks with Chinese officials in Paris as constructive and suggested the delay reflects the Middle East conflict, not a new condition being placed on Beijing.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/j2Zb_lZEZKa9sG8cjMWWbjxLnN-XNfVK_rsBNMu4lO8L2eRvMCp7sS2BjXhSuIceMZ6pAcxe4VRSk-BtKCQteMZGXz3jbCk_yfQ6KqHSw00c40RP9kpwuGp36Sc8zpbxo1h97JIbfYsZCr15EJVwAGdOO1BzoGmkMsGeLrPPRNl8dPRmgBLaHDLn1BHljFlpoBFd48fD_ciUU0yBpPxhNg92iGY' alt='President Trump and Xi Jinping, China’s leader, at their last in-person meeting in Busan, South Korea, in October.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>A familiar pattern: The possible postponement fits a broader Trump habit of making late travel-plan changes that leave both allies and rivals guessing about when high-level meetings will actually happen.</li><li>Why Hormuz matters to China: China imported about 12 million barrels of oil a day in the first two months of 2026, the most in the world, so any disruption around Hormuz carries extra weight for Beijing.</li><li>Not much time to adjust: The summit was due to start in just over two weeks when Trump floated a delay, leaving relatively little room to quietly reschedule a leader-level visit.</li><li>A show of unity at home: President Trump appeared publicly with Vice-President JD Vance for the first time in two weeks as both men denied any split over the Iran war and projected a united front.</li></ul><blockquote>Because of the war I want to be here, I have to be here, I feel. And so we’ve requested that we delay it a month or so. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House: Press secretary Karoline Leavitt said the President still looks forward to visiting China and that the dates may shift because his immediate duty is overseeing the Iran operation. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-timing-of-trump-xi-talks-may-be-moved-white-house-says'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>President Trump: He said he asked for roughly a one-month delay because he believes it is important to remain in Washington during the Iran war, and he also suggested China could help keep passage through Hormuz safe. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/16/world/middleeast/trump-visit-xi-china-iran.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent: Bessent described his Paris discussions with Chinese officials as constructive and indicated that the trip delay is best understood as a response to the Middle East conflict, not as a bargaining tactic toward Beijing. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/16/2026/us-sends-mixed-messages-over-china-summit'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>Chinese government: China’s embassy in Washington did not immediately respond to requests for comment, and Beijing had not directly answered President Trump’s request for help on Hormuz, according to the reports. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/trump-seeks-to-delay-meeting-with-chinas-xi/'>Michael West Media</a>)</li><li>European countries: Several European governments rejected President Trump’s call to help reopen the Strait of Hormuz, underscoring how little international backing that specific request has drawn. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/17/iran-war-live-updates-news-israel-trump-strikes-us-embassy-baghdad-strait-of-hormuz-middle-east-latest'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1982863/white-house-hints-at-delay-in-xi-trump-meeting'>White House hints at delay in Xi-Trump meeting</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/trump-seeks-to-delay-meeting-with-chinas-xi/'>Trump seeks to delay meeting with China’s Xi</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/16/trump-china-summit-iran-war'>Trump seeks to delay China summit as Vance denies ‘wedge’ over Iran war</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/16/2026/us-sends-mixed-messages-over-china-summit'>US sends mixed messages over China summit</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/16/world/iran-war-trump-oil-lebanon'>Trump Says He Wants to Delay Visit to China Because of Middle East Conflict</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-timing-of-trump-xi-talks-may-be-moved-white-house-says'>WATCH: Timing of Trump-Xi talks may be moved, White House says</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trumps-delay-of-xi-visit-echoes-pattern-of-last-minute-changes'>Trump’s delay of Xi visit echoes pattern of last-minute changes</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/article/3346807/trump-pressures-china-over-hormuz-experts-see-possible-delay-beijing-summit'>Trump says the US has requested that China delay Beijing summit by ‘a month or so’</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-asks-china-to-delay-xi-summit-as-iran-war-rages/article70751703.ece'>Trump asks China to delay Xi summit as Iran war rages</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/xi-can-wait-trump-delays-china-visit-an-a